WEBVTT

00:27.350 --> 00:28.610
Get out of here. Quick.

00:29.620 --> 00:30.680
Take precautions!

00:31.920 --> 00:32.710
Hurry and go!

00:33.150 --> 00:34.700
Hurry, or you'll all die.

00:35.480 --> 00:35.950
Go!

00:37.520 --> 00:38.490
Don't go in.

00:38.670 --> 00:40.150
You'll die if you touch those things.

00:40.150 --> 00:40.960
They won't touch us.

00:40.960 --> 00:41.420
Don't go in.

00:41.420 --> 00:42.150
Don't worry.

00:42.820 --> 00:44.280
-Don't go in.
-Don't go in.

01:12.170 --> 01:14.100
There's a stench of rotting flesh.

01:18.020 --> 01:18.780
Shrimpie.

01:18.070 --> 01:22.280
[Inside the Ming Dynasty Shipwreck]

01:18.800 --> 01:20.590
Look, the ship's turned to stone.

01:20.590 --> 01:21.930
The reef and the hull are stuck together.

01:21.930 --> 01:22.789
We can barely see anything.

01:22.789 --> 01:25.760
It really looks like a sunken ship
from the Ming Dynasty.

01:25.760 --> 01:26.690
Stop analyzing.

01:26.870 --> 01:28.480
It's surrounded by seawater.

01:28.480 --> 01:29.310
It's been here too long

01:29.310 --> 01:30.840
and could easily collapse.

01:31.039 --> 01:32.170
Let's move quickly.

01:42.270 --> 01:44.530
The bodies in these bags have all rotted.

01:46.259 --> 01:46.810
Why did the ancient people

01:46.810 --> 01:48.450
hang up these corpses?

01:49.520 --> 01:50.509
Look here.

01:51.229 --> 01:52.660
If I'm not mistaken,

01:52.700 --> 01:54.000
they hung up the bodies

01:54.200 --> 01:55.690
to collect bodily fluids

01:55.970 --> 01:57.500
and nourish these plants.

02:17.500 --> 02:19.230
A Ming Dynasty nautical chart.

02:19.930 --> 02:22.260
No wonder these corpses rotted like that.

02:22.780 --> 02:25.110
It might belong
to the crew from that time.

02:25.370 --> 02:27.770
They probably hung
these body bags up, too.

02:28.450 --> 02:30.000
[On the day of departure, the sea
and sky were clear, and the waters were calm]

02:30.000 --> 02:31.500
[More than a hundred people aboard
attended to their duties in good order]

02:32.650 --> 02:34.540
It also records a strange event.

02:34.660 --> 02:36.130
[On the seventh day of the voyage,
strange things happened]

02:36.360 --> 02:38.560
It says that when the ship set sail,

02:38.579 --> 02:41.110
the crew suddenly began
to die mysteriously.

02:42.120 --> 02:43.410
Each victim developed
red rashes across the body

02:43.410 --> 02:45.240
and died as their flesh
gradually ulcerated.

02:45.240 --> 02:46.960
As more and more people died,

02:47.150 --> 02:48.780
the whole crew panicked.

02:49.240 --> 02:50.500
What's wrong, Mr. San?

02:50.560 --> 02:51.290
This ship...

02:52.090 --> 02:53.960
This ship is haunted by water ghosts.

02:53.960 --> 02:56.060
Water ghosts. The water ghosts are here!

02:56.060 --> 02:57.950
The souls of those you sank into the sea

02:57.950 --> 03:00.900
will be trapped upon the waters,
unable to return home.

03:00.900 --> 03:01.500
So,

03:02.120 --> 03:03.310
they turned into evil spirits

03:03.310 --> 03:05.390
and came back
to the ship to claim our lives!

03:05.390 --> 03:07.200
Mr. San, what should we do?

03:09.150 --> 03:11.280
Hang up all the corpses—

03:11.560 --> 03:13.390
trap the evil spirits inside the corpses.

03:13.390 --> 03:14.290
Once we dock,

03:14.410 --> 03:15.900
give them a proper burial.

03:16.290 --> 03:17.040
Remember,

03:17.120 --> 03:18.210
the feet of the corpses

03:18.210 --> 03:20.140
must never touch the deck.

03:20.310 --> 03:22.570
Black water dripped from these corpses,

03:22.850 --> 03:24.780
which actually worsened the disaster.

03:24.300 --> 03:28.240
[A few months later]

03:46.190 --> 03:47.000
It must be that, back then,

03:47.000 --> 03:49.310
someone on the ship
was poisoned by Twilight Grass.

03:49.310 --> 03:50.980
Those poisoned people

03:51.020 --> 03:52.570
were tainted with the seeds
of Twilight Grass.

03:52.570 --> 03:53.850
After they died,

03:54.030 --> 03:55.829
the seeds grew on their corpses.

03:56.240 --> 03:58.930
Twilight Grass likes
a dark and humid environment,

03:58.930 --> 04:00.590
and the cabin perfectly fits.

04:00.710 --> 04:01.530
Day by day,

04:01.650 --> 04:03.280
Twilight Grass spread throughout the ship,

04:03.280 --> 04:05.280
causing tragedy for the whole ship.

04:05.520 --> 04:06.620
This black bodily fluid

04:06.620 --> 04:08.430
must contain Twilight Grass seeds.

04:08.430 --> 04:10.080
Otherwise, there wouldn't be
so many of these plants.

04:10.080 --> 04:11.960
This is the essence of this ship—

04:12.240 --> 04:14.030
the concentrated bodily fluid

04:15.960 --> 04:17.620
of those who died from poison.

04:23.980 --> 04:25.180
What do you want to do?

04:27.010 --> 04:29.610
Those bastards up there
definitely want this.

04:30.600 --> 04:31.930
Such a dangerous thing—

04:32.630 --> 04:34.830
how can we let it stay and harm the world?

04:35.100 --> 04:36.300
Let me disinfect you.

04:36.360 --> 04:38.090
Looks like you're enjoying it.

04:38.240 --> 04:38.860
Really?

04:39.070 --> 04:40.130
Is it that obvious?

04:40.540 --> 04:41.240
You guys,

04:41.330 --> 04:42.390
go help over there!

04:42.690 --> 04:43.130
Hurry!

04:43.680 --> 04:44.100
Go!

04:44.420 --> 04:44.950
Yes, sir.

04:45.000 --> 04:45.530
Yes, sir.

04:48.010 --> 04:49.670
Adjutant Chen, what's wrong?

04:50.680 --> 04:51.700
Why is it such a mess here?

04:51.700 --> 04:53.180
You ordered us to blast the reef cave.

04:53.180 --> 04:54.630
Now that the reef is blown open,

04:54.630 --> 04:55.590
something came out.

04:55.590 --> 04:57.560
Our men suffered heavy casualties.

04:57.560 --> 04:59.490
Did Salty Zhang hurt you like this?

04:59.810 --> 05:00.570
Who?

05:01.300 --> 05:02.150
Salty Zhang.

05:02.750 --> 05:04.950
Your lifelong nemesis.

05:05.870 --> 05:08.190
Salty Zhang...

05:09.660 --> 05:11.620
The Commander and I have worked hard
on this for so many years.

05:11.620 --> 05:13.280
We can't let them take it away.

05:15.190 --> 05:16.840
Even if I die,

05:17.890 --> 05:20.670
I will get those seeds back for you.

05:24.720 --> 05:25.780
Someone is coming.

05:42.220 --> 05:44.100
I should have finished this kid
off just now.

05:44.100 --> 05:45.240
What a mistake.

06:14.630 --> 06:16.430
Burn all the evidence.

06:16.480 --> 06:18.240
Don't let anyone go!

06:32.630 --> 06:34.430
The only exit is blocked by them.

06:49.470 --> 06:51.270
You want to use the bomb
to blow open the hull

06:51.270 --> 06:53.800
and use the shockwave
to blast us into the sea?

06:53.860 --> 06:54.659
You're crazy.

06:54.980 --> 06:55.860
Let's try.

06:56.430 --> 06:57.370
Leave it to fate.

06:58.670 --> 06:59.760
Leave it to fate.

07:14.890 --> 07:16.510
Throw all the bombs over there!

07:16.510 --> 07:17.470
Blow them up!

07:25.220 --> 07:27.020
I didn't expect such heavy fire.

07:27.160 --> 07:27.830
Can this thing

07:27.830 --> 07:28.910
even hold up?

07:29.930 --> 07:31.440
Do you want to go back to Xiacheng?

07:31.440 --> 07:32.900
Nonsense. Of course, I do.

07:37.940 --> 07:38.800
Okay.

07:43.070 --> 07:44.000
What do you mean?

07:44.440 --> 07:45.240
Zhang Hailou.

07:46.880 --> 07:48.480
I don't want to go back there.

07:49.450 --> 07:51.450
I have nothing left to hold me there.

07:53.510 --> 07:54.770
You go back in my place.

07:55.659 --> 07:56.310
Shrimpie,

07:56.580 --> 07:57.630
can you stop—

08:00.870 --> 08:02.730
Zhang Haixia, what are you doing?

08:08.350 --> 08:09.450
Shrimpie,

08:09.770 --> 08:10.920
are you crazy?

09:44.580 --> 09:50.850
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

09:51.310 --> 09:53.890
[Episode 3]

10:04.030 --> 10:04.960
Shrimpie.

10:06.030 --> 10:06.820
Shrimpie.

10:10.080 --> 10:10.750
Shrimpie.

10:11.640 --> 10:12.370
Shrimpie.

10:25.000 --> 10:25.670
Shrimpie.

10:26.940 --> 10:27.670
Shrimpie.

10:28.140 --> 10:28.900
Shrimpie.

10:33.700 --> 10:35.030
Shrimpie, stay with me.

10:35.910 --> 10:37.040
I'm taking you home.

10:40.390 --> 10:43.200
Then have you ever thought about
the people around you?

10:43.200 --> 10:44.330
You've had your fun,

10:45.220 --> 10:46.820
but what about the rest of us?

11:30.170 --> 11:32.030
Do you want to go back to Xiacheng?

11:33.390 --> 11:34.790
Nonsense. Of course, I do.

11:34.790 --> 11:36.390
I don't want to go back there.

11:37.170 --> 11:39.170
I have nothing left to hold me there.

11:41.410 --> 11:42.670
You go back in my place.

11:53.410 --> 11:55.270
Zhang Haixia, what are you doing?

12:23.020 --> 12:24.230
[A Hundred Flowers in Bloom]

12:24.270 --> 12:27.670
[A dozen years ago]
[The Zhang Residence, Xiacheng]

12:35.110 --> 12:35.780
Mentor.

12:39.690 --> 12:40.540
Zhang Hailou,

12:40.920 --> 12:42.120
what are you drawing?

12:42.820 --> 12:44.620
A thrush. Looks like one, right?

12:51.200 --> 12:53.860
Zhang Haixia,
what's wrong with your eyebrows?

12:55.610 --> 12:57.140
Go wash off those eyebrows.

13:14.390 --> 13:15.860
This is your true nature.

13:17.320 --> 13:18.890
Your true nature is a snake.

13:19.400 --> 13:20.260
A snake

13:20.480 --> 13:21.880
will devour everything.

13:26.010 --> 13:27.440
But you can't be blamed for this.

13:27.440 --> 13:28.970
Luckily, you had dumb luck,

13:29.250 --> 13:31.110
having Zhang Haixia by your side—

13:31.270 --> 13:32.330
he will remind you.

13:38.910 --> 13:39.910
Did you hear that?

13:40.540 --> 13:41.730
Be nicer to me.

14:09.150 --> 14:09.980
Help!

14:12.600 --> 14:13.580
Help!

14:20.390 --> 14:23.330
[Beilian Wharf]

14:21.290 --> 14:21.950
Commander.

14:22.340 --> 14:24.840
The ship departed
from Panhua Reef half a month ago

14:24.840 --> 14:26.580
and just arrived at the port today.

14:26.580 --> 14:28.910
This is a letter written by Adjutant Chen.

14:31.510 --> 14:32.670
Dear Commander,

14:33.030 --> 14:34.030
after ten years of wandering,

14:34.030 --> 14:35.670
fortunately, I did not fail your trust.

14:35.670 --> 14:37.390
I've obtained the Twilight Grass seeds,

14:37.390 --> 14:39.190
completing your instructions.

14:39.720 --> 14:40.960
Please be careful

14:40.960 --> 14:44.580
of the Southern Archives under
the Maritime Supervisory Office.

14:44.580 --> 14:46.770
The person I encountered at Panhua Reef

14:46.770 --> 14:49.230
was Salty Zhang,
an agent from the Archives.

14:49.410 --> 14:50.270
Additionally,

14:50.530 --> 14:52.480
the Twilight Grass Poison has spread,

14:52.480 --> 14:54.270
infecting all the soldiers in the fleet.

14:54.270 --> 14:56.270
Everyone else has been eliminated.

14:56.530 --> 14:59.060
The soldiers on the ship
must not be kept alive

14:59.250 --> 15:00.780
to prevent future trouble.

15:01.460 --> 15:02.220
Commander,

15:03.100 --> 15:05.290
Adjutant Chen's body has stiffened.

15:05.370 --> 15:06.810
We can't get the jar off.

15:08.360 --> 15:09.650
What is the axe for?

15:10.390 --> 15:11.370
Chop off his hand

15:11.720 --> 15:12.840
and take the jar.

15:23.980 --> 15:25.390
The so-called

15:26.150 --> 15:28.540
[Mo Yungao, Leader
of the Mo Warlord Faction of Beilian]

15:26.360 --> 15:28.940
Southern Archives

15:29.870 --> 15:30.870
under the Nanyang

15:31.890 --> 15:33.620
Maritime Supervisory Office—

15:34.630 --> 15:36.560
investigate it thoroughly, okay?

15:37.120 --> 15:38.330
After finding them,

15:37.220 --> 15:39.610
[Lu Junxiang, Adjutant
in the Mo Warlord Faction of Beilian]

15:38.530 --> 15:40.130
how should we deal with them?

15:42.410 --> 15:44.050
In the letter, he said

15:45.130 --> 15:47.340
that the man is called Salty Zhang.

15:48.460 --> 15:49.670
His surname is Zhang.

16:11.900 --> 16:13.370
A member of the Zhang family.

16:13.370 --> 16:15.610
I have finally found you.

16:28.670 --> 16:31.680
By any means necessary,

16:32.370 --> 16:34.430
find everyone in the Archives for me.

16:48.380 --> 16:54.560
[Mo Yungao's Special Train]

16:48.480 --> 16:49.150
Commander.

16:51.150 --> 16:53.940
I have investigated everywhere.

16:54.650 --> 16:57.050
But didn't find
the so-called Southern Archives.

16:57.050 --> 16:58.700
We caught some people

16:58.720 --> 17:00.620
who are suspected members of the Archives.

17:00.620 --> 17:02.480
Some of them revealed a few clues.

17:14.740 --> 17:15.460
The Southern Archives

17:15.460 --> 17:17.349
is an organization that specializes
in investigating mysterious incidents.

17:17.349 --> 17:19.020
It originated

17:19.119 --> 17:20.780
from an ancient Zhang family.

17:21.200 --> 17:22.069
That family

17:22.250 --> 17:23.310
is very mysterious

17:24.069 --> 17:25.730
and has extraordinary power.

17:27.050 --> 17:28.170
The leader

17:28.690 --> 17:29.780
of the Archives

17:29.810 --> 17:31.110
is Zhang Haiqi.

17:34.550 --> 17:35.850
Zhang Haiqi.

17:38.160 --> 17:39.570
In the Panhua Reef Case,

17:40.240 --> 17:41.420
the advisor's prophecy

17:41.420 --> 17:42.880
was almost fully realized.

17:42.880 --> 17:45.420
The case ended
with two agents critically injured

17:45.420 --> 17:46.820
and remains unresolved.

17:47.200 --> 17:49.060
What they did not expect was that,

17:49.240 --> 17:50.990
during their recovery,

17:51.420 --> 17:53.510
the Balongzhou Branch
of the Southern Archives

17:53.510 --> 17:55.770
was suddenly ordered
to suspend all operations.

17:55.770 --> 17:57.690
All personnel were dismissed

17:58.020 --> 18:00.220
and instructed to recover on their own.

18:02.460 --> 18:06.390
[Notice of Closure—
Maritime Supervisory Office]

18:08.530 --> 18:11.590
Zhang Hailou kept trying
to contact the headquarters,

18:11.820 --> 18:14.450
but never received any reply.

18:39.000 --> 18:41.730
Where have all the people
from the Archives gone?

18:41.920 --> 18:43.720
Why didn't even Mentor respond?

18:46.840 --> 18:50.120
[Balai Rainforest]

18:48.330 --> 18:49.400
Time passed.

18:50.400 --> 18:52.930
In the three years
since the Panhua Reef case,

18:53.020 --> 18:54.570
members of the Southern Archives
in various branches

18:54.570 --> 18:56.980
went missing one after another.

18:58.070 --> 19:00.230
Zhang Haiqi,
the director of the Archives,

19:00.230 --> 19:01.760
has been investigating it.

19:22.700 --> 19:25.620
Who hung those bodies up?

19:25.680 --> 19:26.470
I don't know.

19:26.860 --> 19:28.240
It seems they offended someone

19:28.240 --> 19:31.340
and were hung up in revenge.
They've been hanging for a long time.

19:31.340 --> 19:33.460
I heard they were still alive
when they were just hung up.

19:33.460 --> 19:35.660
Their screams could be heard every day.

19:37.280 --> 19:38.480
Drive the car over.

20:25.520 --> 20:27.920
Why did you kill the people
of the Archives?

20:51.970 --> 20:53.130
Who are you?

20:53.230 --> 20:54.410
Who betrayed the Archives?

20:54.410 --> 20:55.800
You don't need to know.

20:55.830 --> 20:57.210
You won't live anyway.

21:26.710 --> 21:29.240
I won't let you die
without knowing the truth.

21:30.600 --> 21:32.970
[Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office]

21:44.940 --> 21:54.410
[Nanyang Daily]

21:56.720 --> 21:59.120
Are you still thinking about these things?

22:02.380 --> 22:03.220
Over the years,

22:03.220 --> 22:05.900
I've looked into many plants related
to Twilight Grass.

22:05.900 --> 22:07.100
But later, I found out

22:07.160 --> 22:08.400
that the last time Twilight Grass appeared

22:08.400 --> 22:10.000
was in the late Ming Dynasty.

22:10.380 --> 22:11.590
This grass, from root to seed,

22:11.590 --> 22:12.520
is highly toxic.

22:12.980 --> 22:14.000
The fact that we survived

22:14.000 --> 22:15.660
is nothing short of a miracle.

22:16.720 --> 22:18.850
It's been so long since this happened.

22:19.530 --> 22:21.860
Is it meaningful
for you to think about it?

22:25.700 --> 22:26.380
How is it?

22:27.160 --> 22:28.850
Still no news from headquarters?

22:28.850 --> 22:30.060
Not only no news,

22:30.290 --> 22:31.670
but they haven't even paid us.

22:31.670 --> 22:34.130
Do you think the Archives
will be disbanded?

22:34.240 --> 22:35.340
If it is disbanded,

22:35.940 --> 22:37.070
what are your plans?

22:37.180 --> 22:38.010
I think

22:38.450 --> 22:41.980
we need to go back to Xiacheng
to find Mentor as soon as possible.

22:42.570 --> 22:43.710
If it weren't for me,

22:44.570 --> 22:46.350
you could have gone back
to Xiacheng a long time ago.

22:46.350 --> 22:47.480
Don't say that.

22:47.960 --> 22:50.240
When we get back
to Xiacheng and find Mentor,

22:50.240 --> 22:51.000
I'm sure she'll

22:51.000 --> 22:52.330
be able to cure your leg.

23:00.400 --> 23:01.630
Even if she can't,

23:02.080 --> 23:03.080
you still have me.

23:05.400 --> 23:07.660
I'll take care of you
till the day you die.

23:10.900 --> 23:12.030
My leg

23:12.530 --> 23:13.510
cannot be cured.

23:14.980 --> 23:15.980
One day,

23:16.770 --> 23:18.500
you will have to act on your own.

23:18.960 --> 23:20.220
I won't be by your side.

23:20.640 --> 23:22.440
No one will be watching over you.

23:23.240 --> 23:24.610
I can just quit my job.

23:24.750 --> 23:25.810
You are so capable.

23:27.070 --> 23:28.470
It'd be a pity if you quit.

23:29.080 --> 23:30.880
What's the use of being capable?

23:31.110 --> 23:32.570
I made you end up like this.

23:34.790 --> 23:36.140
Actually, it's not too late

23:36.140 --> 23:37.480
for you to understand all this now.

23:37.480 --> 23:38.780
You still have a long way to go.

23:38.780 --> 23:40.580
You have to keep moving forward.

23:44.220 --> 23:46.750
Just tell me what you want to say.
I'll listen.

23:47.390 --> 23:49.410
When you encounter something
in the future,

23:49.410 --> 23:50.470
you must stay calm.

23:50.930 --> 23:52.130
Never act on impulse.

23:53.640 --> 23:56.570
Think about
how it will affect the people around you.

23:56.700 --> 23:57.350
Got it.

24:15.550 --> 24:16.360
I'm sorry.

24:26.030 --> 24:26.760
Look at this.

24:27.530 --> 24:28.310
Do you like it?

24:28.310 --> 24:29.320
No, thank you.

24:37.970 --> 24:39.300
Newspaper! Newspaper!

24:39.300 --> 24:41.680
Mysterious toxic plant spreads rapidly.

24:41.710 --> 24:44.710
-Many people have died of poisoning in Xucheng!
-Kid.

24:45.060 --> 24:46.260
I'll get a newspaper.

24:47.720 --> 24:49.000
Newspaper! Newspaper!

24:49.000 --> 24:51.610
Mysterious toxic plant spreads rapidly.

24:50.250 --> 24:51.540
[Nanyang Daily]

24:51.720 --> 24:54.870
Many people have died
of poisoning in Xucheng!

24:57.910 --> 24:59.440
We've got business. Hurry.

25:01.050 --> 25:02.320
Look at this.

25:03.070 --> 25:04.250
Is it exactly what I thought?

25:04.250 --> 25:06.030
We're out of money. Why are you
buying so many newspapers?

25:06.030 --> 25:08.560
Didn't I pick up a bunch
of newspapers for you?

25:12.480 --> 25:13.750
A bizarre disease suddenly

25:13.750 --> 25:14.980
broke out in Xucheng.

25:15.030 --> 25:16.780
Resembles...

25:17.250 --> 25:17.860
[Resembles a dandelion]

25:20.920 --> 25:22.350
A large number of red rashes
appear all over the body,

25:22.180 --> 25:22.820
[It is highly lethal]

25:22.380 --> 25:23.690
accompanied by ulceration.

25:23.690 --> 25:24.190
[Some victims may die instantly]

25:23.850 --> 25:26.090
Death occurs rapidly after inhalation.

25:26.090 --> 25:27.110
Twilight Grass.

25:27.850 --> 25:29.110
It's been three years.

25:30.290 --> 25:31.940
We are the only two

25:32.110 --> 25:33.330
who survived the Panhua Reef,

25:33.330 --> 25:34.590
apart from those warlords.

25:34.590 --> 25:36.590
I've been looking up information
on the Twilight Grass all these years,

25:36.590 --> 25:37.750
but with no results.

25:38.440 --> 25:40.040
Now it has finally appeared.

25:40.530 --> 25:42.000
Those bastards are back.

25:45.530 --> 25:47.000
What are they up to?

25:49.010 --> 25:51.940
The Evil God case was connected
to the warlords, too.

25:52.720 --> 25:54.720
Maybe these two things are related.

26:03.530 --> 26:04.310
Forget it.

26:05.220 --> 26:07.140
The Archives are gone.
Why should I investigate?

26:07.140 --> 26:08.800
What does it have to do with me?

26:14.270 --> 26:16.250
The shipping in Nanyang
is very developed now.

26:16.250 --> 26:18.810
Thousands of people
pass through every dock every day.

26:18.810 --> 26:20.700
If it really is the Twilight Grass,

26:20.700 --> 26:21.810
those stamens,

26:22.000 --> 26:23.730
filaments, and seeds

26:23.770 --> 26:25.140
will be brought to various places.

26:25.140 --> 26:26.510
They are all highly toxic

26:26.510 --> 26:28.500
and will endanger ordinary people.

26:28.500 --> 26:30.680
Although we haven't been paid
for a long time,

26:30.680 --> 26:31.410
the Archives

26:31.420 --> 26:33.350
still has a duty to issue warnings.

26:33.830 --> 26:36.830
You don't want those people
to suffer, either, do you?

26:40.160 --> 26:41.890
Why don't you go and take a look?

26:45.540 --> 26:46.850
I'll be back quickly.

27:08.010 --> 27:12.080
[The Xucheng Twilight Grass Poison Case]

28:28.880 --> 28:29.620
Shrimpie.

28:32.830 --> 28:34.030
We're here. Get down.

28:37.240 --> 28:38.270
Wait here a minute.

28:38.270 --> 28:39.670
I'll go get a seat for you.

28:41.570 --> 28:42.670
What's going on?

28:43.030 --> 28:44.890
Don't worry. She's not poisoned.

28:45.460 --> 28:47.440
I waited for her
outside the city for three days.

28:47.440 --> 28:48.920
She's already been disinfected

28:48.920 --> 28:49.830
and bathed.

28:51.310 --> 28:52.790
We're both familiar with this poison.

28:52.790 --> 28:54.050
If she were poisoned,

28:54.160 --> 28:56.750
ulceration would definitely appear
within three days.

28:56.750 --> 28:57.410
Have a seat.

29:01.660 --> 29:02.860
She's Zhang Haijiao.

29:04.180 --> 29:05.580
Call him Uncle Shrimpie.

29:05.720 --> 29:06.880
Uncle Shrimpie.

29:11.460 --> 29:13.320
You named the younger generation

29:13.460 --> 29:15.010
using characters from our own generation?

29:15.010 --> 29:15.960
Mentor said

29:16.070 --> 29:18.460
that those living abroad can take "Hai"
as their generation name

29:18.460 --> 29:21.290
to signify their separation from home
and their wandering lives.

29:21.290 --> 29:22.220
Are you thirsty?

29:23.680 --> 29:26.540
Separation from home
and their wandering lives...

29:32.850 --> 29:34.220
My name is Zhang Haixia.

29:35.530 --> 29:37.190
"Xia," as in a wandering hero.

29:38.770 --> 29:40.170
His name is Zhang Hailou.

29:40.330 --> 29:41.390
"Lou," as in tower.

29:41.640 --> 29:43.640
Listening to the spring rain
through the night in a little tower.

29:43.640 --> 29:46.100
A wandering hero of Xianyang
for many years.

29:47.960 --> 29:49.290
Is that a line of poetry?

29:50.420 --> 29:51.700
I meant for you to fan her.

29:51.700 --> 29:52.160
Fine.

29:56.980 --> 29:58.240
To welcome Haijiao,

29:58.460 --> 29:59.990
we are having hotpot today.

30:06.640 --> 30:08.170
Thank you, Uncle Shrimpie.

30:10.370 --> 30:11.900
Thank you, Uncle Shrimpie.

30:32.590 --> 30:33.510
These three villages

30:33.510 --> 30:36.310
were the first places where Twilight Grass
spread simultaneously.

30:36.310 --> 30:37.470
In there,

30:37.290 --> 30:38.990
[When did they get poisoned?]
[July 2] [First Victim]

30:37.700 --> 30:38.840
the first victims

30:38.870 --> 30:40.700
all had boarded Nan'an

30:39.110 --> 30:42.440
[The Nan'an]

30:40.880 --> 30:43.540
from Xiacheng to Balai
in the first week of July.

30:48.740 --> 30:50.420
I've checked the news in Xiacheng—

30:50.420 --> 30:52.160
no one was poisoned by the Twilight Grass.

30:52.160 --> 30:53.040
This means

30:53.090 --> 30:55.800
these three people must
have been poisoned aboard the ship.

30:55.800 --> 30:56.650
You can take a closer look

30:56.160 --> 30:58.050
[Yeruicheng] [Yungangyi] [Langhuacheng]

30:56.680 --> 30:58.120
at the locations of these villages.

30:58.120 --> 30:59.670
[Balai] [Xucheng]

30:59.610 --> 31:01.090
They are evenly
distributed around Xucheng.

30:59.670 --> 31:08.540
[Yeruicheng] [Yungangyi] [Langhuacheng]

31:02.050 --> 31:02.740
I think someone

31:02.740 --> 31:04.380
deliberately found these three people

31:04.380 --> 31:05.780
and had them carry Twilight Grass Poison

31:05.780 --> 31:07.140
back to their villages at the same time,

31:07.140 --> 31:08.250
so that the toxic weed could spread

31:08.250 --> 31:09.580
as quickly as possible.

31:09.850 --> 31:10.780
If this incident

31:11.160 --> 31:13.740
was also the work of the warlord
who dug up the Twilight Grass back then,

31:13.740 --> 31:15.830
their people are likely on Nan'an.

31:16.920 --> 31:19.060
[When did they get poisoned?]
[July 2] [First Victim]

31:32.680 --> 31:34.880
Since all clues now point to Nan'an,

31:36.140 --> 31:38.470
should we get on the ship and investigate?

31:39.220 --> 31:40.330
When will it dock again?

31:40.330 --> 31:40.930
Next week.

31:45.660 --> 31:47.320
The Nan'an heads to Xiacheng.

31:47.660 --> 31:49.180
If you want to investigate,

31:49.180 --> 31:50.640
you have to go the whole way

31:51.110 --> 31:52.440
and get off at Xiacheng.

32:01.250 --> 32:03.030
The tickets for Nan'an
are very expensive.

32:03.030 --> 32:05.050
Even with a one-way steerage ticket,

32:05.050 --> 32:07.140
our money is only enough for one.

32:07.420 --> 32:08.840
And by the time you come back,

32:08.840 --> 32:10.100
it will be a year later,

32:10.110 --> 32:10.690
right?

32:10.980 --> 32:12.050
You don't need to worry about that.

32:12.050 --> 32:13.780
I've already thought about it.

32:15.400 --> 32:16.600
If we sell this place,

32:16.660 --> 32:18.680
we can buy two tickets
and go back to Xiacheng together.

32:18.680 --> 32:19.240
And

32:19.810 --> 32:21.330
we can return to Xiacheng
in the name of investigating a case.

32:21.330 --> 32:22.510
That way, we definitely won't
be considered deserters.

32:22.510 --> 32:23.730
Sell the Archives?

32:24.350 --> 32:25.940
How could you come up with such an idea?

32:25.940 --> 32:26.510
Why not?

32:26.540 --> 32:27.980
Why don't you just sell me instead?

32:27.980 --> 32:30.840
Hey, this place has
been abandoned for three years.

32:30.880 --> 32:32.530
They are just worldly possessions.

32:32.530 --> 32:35.130
We have to think
about the living first, right?

32:39.110 --> 32:39.850
You go back.

32:42.030 --> 32:44.890
Go back and check
why our salaries haven't arrived.

32:45.160 --> 32:47.160
And visit Mentor while you're at it.

32:54.840 --> 32:56.700
If the Southern Archives is gone,

32:59.770 --> 33:00.830
don't come back.

33:06.210 --> 33:07.270
Send me a telegram,

33:08.510 --> 33:09.640
and we'll part ways.

33:09.980 --> 33:10.910
Absolutely not.

33:11.510 --> 33:13.170
We agreed to go back together.

33:13.510 --> 33:15.840
It would be so awkward
if I went back alone.

33:16.550 --> 33:18.480
And the money belongs to both of us.

33:18.530 --> 33:19.460
You have a share.

33:25.500 --> 33:26.630
I've made up my mind.

33:26.930 --> 33:27.990
I'm not going back.

33:29.570 --> 33:30.570
You go back for me.

33:31.460 --> 33:34.060
There's no need
to waste your life here with me.

33:37.380 --> 33:38.070
Forget it.

33:39.530 --> 33:42.130
I'll investigate
those three villages first.

33:43.530 --> 33:44.660
Maybe you're right.

33:46.590 --> 33:49.320
This way, neither of us
has to go back to Xiacheng.

33:50.460 --> 33:51.190
That's good.

34:08.050 --> 34:08.610
Hailou,

34:09.130 --> 34:10.790
you still have a long way to go.

34:11.020 --> 34:12.820
You have to keep moving forward.

34:14.260 --> 34:16.719
When we get back
to Xiacheng and find Mentor,

34:16.750 --> 34:18.949
I'm sure she'll be able to cure your leg.

34:43.780 --> 34:45.580
You've already switched sides?

34:46.510 --> 34:48.770
Have you forgotten who brought you back?

34:49.380 --> 34:50.510
Uncle Shrimpie said

34:50.630 --> 34:52.760
you really want to go back to Xiacheng.

34:53.010 --> 34:55.860
It's not easy to have something
you want to do in mind.

34:55.860 --> 34:57.190
He envies you very much.

34:57.260 --> 34:58.790
So you want to drive me away?

34:59.030 --> 34:59.880
Didn't you say

35:00.380 --> 35:01.460
you brought me back

35:01.500 --> 35:03.900
just to serve Uncle Shrimpie
like my own father?

35:03.900 --> 35:05.430
I will take good care of him.

35:05.730 --> 35:07.990
You can leave without worrying about us.

35:08.610 --> 35:10.870
Did Shrimpie Zhang teach you to say that?

35:13.800 --> 35:15.440
This is also my own idea.

35:16.300 --> 35:19.070
In the future, Uncle Shrimpie
and I will depend on each other.

35:19.070 --> 35:20.650
We will work hard on our business.

35:20.650 --> 35:22.110
When we save enough money,

35:22.300 --> 35:24.360
we will come to Xiacheng
to reunite with you.

35:24.360 --> 35:26.090
You can leave without worrying about us.

35:26.090 --> 35:27.490
We won't die without you.

35:36.260 --> 35:38.460
Zhang Haixia, what's the point of this?

35:42.530 --> 35:43.500
You're not dead.

35:47.440 --> 35:48.450
You were expelled from the Archives,

35:48.450 --> 35:50.850
and you still have the nerve
to show up here?

35:51.130 --> 35:52.230
Do I have to send you to prison,

35:52.230 --> 35:53.630
or will you go on your own?

35:55.690 --> 35:56.690
Don't act rashly.

35:58.460 --> 35:59.860
Call him Mr. Zhang Ruipu.

36:00.360 --> 36:01.760
According to seniority,

36:01.860 --> 36:03.390
he is even Mentor's senior.

36:14.380 --> 36:17.040
I heard you're looking
into the Twilight Grass.

36:17.820 --> 36:19.550
So I came specifically to help.

36:23.670 --> 36:24.600
Long time no see.

36:41.670 --> 36:43.330
A master from the common folk?

36:44.860 --> 36:46.660
Turns out you're actually poor.

36:46.960 --> 36:49.290
Mr. Zhang, beat us
or kill us as you please.

36:49.530 --> 36:50.690
Why mock us?

36:51.190 --> 36:53.010
I just think your spirit is commendable.

36:53.010 --> 36:55.470
So poor, yet you
still work for the Archives.

36:57.570 --> 36:58.360
Actually, the first time

36:58.360 --> 37:00.420
you appeared under that saline lake,

37:00.960 --> 37:02.760
I had already known who you were.

37:03.170 --> 37:05.230
But I felt that with your qualities,

37:05.860 --> 37:07.480
you'd never catch me.

37:07.730 --> 37:09.190
So I didn't eliminate you,

37:09.500 --> 37:10.840
lest the Southern Archives

37:10.840 --> 37:12.300
send some reliable people

37:13.260 --> 37:15.060
and leave me no peace in Xucheng.

37:16.190 --> 37:17.000
As a result,

37:17.500 --> 37:19.030
living up to expectations,

37:19.050 --> 37:20.780
you were even more incompetent

37:21.300 --> 37:22.710
than I expected.

37:24.340 --> 37:27.050
Actually, last time, we were
investigating the Evil God Case.

37:27.050 --> 37:28.710
Tricking you was just a bonus.

37:29.600 --> 37:30.300
By the way,

37:30.670 --> 37:31.980
how much do you know

37:31.980 --> 37:34.180
about this Twilight Grass Poison case?

37:44.650 --> 37:46.130
Don't waste my time.

37:46.260 --> 37:47.070
Zhang Hailou.

37:48.050 --> 37:50.360
Twilight Grass hasn't appeared
for hundreds of years.

37:50.360 --> 37:52.490
This time, it suddenly
broke out in Xucheng,

37:52.490 --> 37:55.020
yet you came back alive
from a heap of corpses.

37:55.230 --> 37:56.190
As far as I know,

37:56.260 --> 37:58.230
only those who have been
exposed to Twilight Grass

37:58.230 --> 38:01.110
can develop
an alkaloid barrier in their bodies.

38:01.550 --> 38:03.110
How were you exposed to it?

38:14.900 --> 38:17.760
Your brother-in-arms
was crippled because of you.

38:18.570 --> 38:20.630
You've taken care of him until now...

38:22.210 --> 38:23.710
Are you a bit tired of it?

38:25.840 --> 38:27.170
If there's an accident,

38:28.210 --> 38:29.130
for example,

38:30.440 --> 38:31.780
I help you kill him,

38:39.820 --> 38:42.050
would your life be a bit easier?

38:55.170 --> 38:56.440
Since you were from the Archives,

38:56.440 --> 38:58.170
you should know the rules of it.

39:00.510 --> 39:03.040
The Southern Archives' rule
has always been:

39:03.050 --> 39:04.180
what must not be said

39:04.690 --> 39:07.620
will not be said,
even if one's closest kin dies right

39:08.780 --> 39:09.840
before their eyes.

39:10.360 --> 39:12.220
How can you threaten me with this?

39:13.150 --> 39:13.980
You keep him.

39:15.150 --> 39:15.880
I'm leaving.

39:43.050 --> 39:43.880
Zhang Ruipu!

40:19.170 --> 40:20.480
How touching.

40:21.830 --> 40:22.710
I'm envious.

40:25.340 --> 40:27.020
Then I suppose it's time
to start extracting answers.

40:27.020 --> 40:28.210
Answer me,

40:29.130 --> 40:30.790
or I start snapping his spine,

40:30.790 --> 40:32.550
vertebrae by vertebrae.

40:33.010 --> 40:34.740
For every minute you hesitate,

40:35.710 --> 40:37.070
I'll crush another one.

40:38.510 --> 40:40.300
Right now, his arms still have feeling.

40:40.300 --> 40:41.750
In seven minutes,

40:42.920 --> 40:44.390
other than his head...

40:44.940 --> 40:45.690
No,

40:45.820 --> 40:47.690
he'll only be able to move his head.
